## Current version

wf-roadmap-item-wolfmed = Wolfmed
wf-roadmap-item-wolfmed-desc = Damage lands on body parts as wounds: cuts, bruises, burns, fractures and bleeds, with pain, infections and organ damage. Limbs come off and go back on, and medics get autodoc pods, IV drips and a new health analyzer.
wf-roadmap-item-planets = Planets and caverns
wf-roadmap-item-planets-desc = Orbit the worlds of the Kyphrus system, land or crash on them, and climb down into their caverns. With weather, day and night, pressurised rooms, stairs and atmospheric jetpacks.
wf-roadmap-item-encounters = Random encounters
wf-roadmap-item-encounters-desc = NPC-crewed ships roam the sector: patrols, freighters, pirates, wandering traders and fleet battles. Patrols warn you off before they open fire, ships in distress pay for help (or are bait), and derelict hulks can be cleared and claimed.
wf-roadmap-item-ship-shields = Ship shields
wf-roadmap-item-ship-shields-desc = A reworked shield with new effects that also stops collisions, flak and mines. Shunt it toward one side for stronger cover there.
wf-roadmap-item-species = New species
wf-roadmap-item-species-desc = New playable species from HardLight and Starlight, including Avali, Shadekin and Protogens, plus Wolfgate's own Canines, with their own markings, voices, languages and medicine.
wf-roadmap-item-anatomy = Anatomy system
wf-roadmap-item-anatomy-desc = Opt-in character anatomy, set in the character creator's Anatomy tab and adjustable in round. It is consent-gated: others only see or change it with your consent and their own adult content setting on.
wf-roadmap-item-custom-markings = Custom markings
wf-roadmap-item-custom-markings-desc = Draw your own markings in a pixel editor or import a PNG, animate them, and wear up to four on a character.
wf-roadmap-item-appearance = Appearance options
wf-roadmap-item-appearance-desc = Mismatched species parts, an eye marking category, digitigrade or plantigrade legs, and all of NovaSector's markings.
wf-roadmap-item-tractor-beams = Tractor beams
wf-roadmap-item-tractor-beams-desc = Hold, reel in or lock another ship or loose debris with a powered dish and console, no docking needed.
wf-roadmap-item-ship-consoles = Ship console upgrades
wf-roadmap-item-ship-consoles-desc = A whole-ship view with hull telemetry, a collision warning that calls out hard impacts before they happen, and hull cameras with a low-light feed.
wf-roadmap-item-pilot-view = External pilot view
wf-roadmap-item-pilot-view-desc = See your whole ship from outside while at the helm. Drag with the right mouse button to pan and scroll to zoom.
wf-roadmap-item-deposit-boxes = Safety deposit boxes
wf-roadmap-item-deposit-boxes-desc = Buy a small, medium or large box at the console and it keeps your valuables between rounds. Ported from Wayfarer.
wf-roadmap-item-shockwaves = Explosion shockwaves
wf-roadmap-item-shockwaves-desc = Explosions throw out a visible shockwave that shoves people and loose objects away from the blast.
wf-roadmap-item-job-titles = Custom job titles
wf-roadmap-item-job-titles-desc = Contractors can write their own job title, which goes on their ID card and station records.
wf-roadmap-item-ship-pa = Ship PA system
wf-roadmap-item-ship-pa-desc = Speakers, situation codes and general quarters, run from the ship console.
wf-roadmap-item-ship-access = Ship access
wf-roadmap-item-ship-access-desc = Ship doors run on ordinary airlock access. Whoever holds the deed owns the ship and decides who gets in.
wf-roadmap-item-traders = NPC traders
wf-roadmap-item-traders-desc = Traders you talk to on Caelestinus Central: shops, a shipyard dealer, a used ship salesman and a fuel technician.
wf-roadmap-item-classic-vessels = Classic vessels
wf-roadmap-item-classic-vessels-desc = Over a hundred classic ships are back in the shipyards, with a filter to find them.
wf-roadmap-item-dredger = The Dredger
wf-roadmap-item-dredger-desc = A salvage-class ship, with its own plushie.
wf-roadmap-item-tethers = Ropes and harpoons
wf-roadmap-item-tethers-desc = Ropes, anchor eyes, a ship harpoon turret and power cords between grids.
wf-roadmap-item-interface = Wolfgate interface
wf-roadmap-item-interface-desc = A new lobby, character creator and HUD, with Futurist and Retro skins.
wf-roadmap-item-prediction = Projectile prediction
wf-roadmap-item-prediction-desc = Your own shots leave the barrel the moment you fire. Ported from RMC-14.
wf-roadmap-item-heat-haze = Heat haze
wf-roadmap-item-heat-haze-desc = Hot air shimmers over fires and superheated rooms.
wf-roadmap-item-blood-trails = Blood trails
wf-roadmap-item-blood-trails-desc = Step in blood and you leave footprints. Drag or crawl with a wound and you leave a trail. A mop or space cleaner takes them off. Ported from Colonial Marines Universe.
wf-roadmap-item-emote-voices = Scream and laugh voices
wf-roadmap-item-emote-voices-desc = Pick your character's scream and laugh in the character editor.
wf-roadmap-item-subtle = Subtle emotes
wf-roadmap-item-subtle-desc = An emote only the people right next to you see, hidden from ghosts. Use the right click menu or /subtle.
wf-roadmap-item-headshots = Headshots
wf-roadmap-item-headshots-desc = Character headshots in the examine window.
wf-roadmap-item-avali = Avali medicine and clothing
wf-roadmap-item-avali-feathers = Avali feathers and flight
wf-roadmap-item-avali-feathers-desc = Avali preen wearable feathers that work as quills, fly between levels like moths, and have their own organs and printable limbs.
wf-roadmap-item-fire-sprites = New fire sprites
wf-roadmap-item-fire-sprites-desc = Burning people and objects use TauCeti's fire sprites.
wf-roadmap-item-resprites = New sprites
wf-roadmap-item-resprites-desc = Fresh sprites for floor tiles, cryo tubes, freezers, hydroponics and gas overlays.
wf-roadmap-item-cc-medbay = Caelestinus Central medbay
wf-roadmap-item-cc-medbay-desc = A rebuilt medical wing on Caelestinus Central.

## Upcoming

wf-roadmap-item-encounters-fleets = Encounters: fleets and crews
wf-roadmap-item-encounters-fleets-desc = Frigate and capital ship patrols, a named pirate band, crews with faction names, accents and ID cards, and engineers who keep a ship's reactor running.
wf-roadmap-item-planet-structures = Random planet structures
wf-roadmap-item-planet-structures-desc = Randomly generated structures across planet surfaces, different every round, to find and explore.

## Future versions

wf-roadmap-item-planet-cracking = Planet cracking
wf-roadmap-item-planet-cracking-desc = Builds on planets and caverns, as its own update.
wf-roadmap-item-outposts-bases = Outposts: persistent bases
wf-roadmap-item-outposts-bases-desc = Found a base on a planet with an Outpost Console and build it up. It saves to your character, and you can bring it back in a later round.
wf-roadmap-item-outposts-economy = Outposts: economy
wf-roadmap-item-outposts-economy-desc = An outpost kit, a fabricator for prefab walls and machines, wind, solar and fuel power, and a trade hub that drops orders in by parachute. No ship needed once you are down.
wf-roadmap-item-outposts-living = Outposts: living there
wf-roadmap-item-outposts-living-desc = Spawn in your outpost's cryopod, and open positions so friends can join you there.
wf-roadmap-item-outposts-raids = Outposts: raids and POIs
wf-roadmap-item-outposts-raids-desc = Worlds with edges and points of interest to explore and claim, night raids by wildlife and raiders who breach walls, early warning and turrets.
wf-roadmap-item-outposts-more = Outposts: farming and more
wf-roadmap-item-outposts-more-desc = Shuttle crash starts, play groups, landing pads, farming and livestock, orbital defence and basements.
wf-roadmap-item-encounters-scanner = Encounters: scanner contacts
wf-roadmap-item-encounters-scanner-desc = Encounter ships cross the sector as mass scanner blips and only spawn when you close in.
wf-roadmap-item-encounters-freight = Encounters: freight value
wf-roadmap-item-encounters-freight-desc = Freighters in value brackets, from low-value haulers to military and nuclear transports. The richer the cargo, the heavier the defences, and boarding one intact pays better than destroying it.
wf-roadmap-item-encounters-follow-ups = Encounters: follow-ups
wf-roadmap-item-encounters-follow-ups-desc = One encounter sets up the next: destroy a freighter and a patrol comes looking along its route.
